KNOWNBUG
main.c
--arrays-uf-always
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With --arrays-uf-always, a read from a two-dimensional array at indices that
equal the indices of a preceding write, but are different terms, is not
constrained to yield the written value: the propositional back-end reports a
spurious counterexample. Without --arrays-uf-always, and with --z3, the
assertion is proved.
